// VOLD_variant_removed.schema — OLD: Tier {Bronze, Silver, Gold}
//
// One of the fixed form's UNLAWFUL lineage rows (docs/FIXED-FORM-VERSIONING-TESTS.md,
// internal/fixedunlawful). The OLD and the NEW file of this pair differ by
// EXACTLY Tier {Bronze, Silver, Gold} -> {Bronze, Gold}. `lead` and `trail` bracket the row's field.
//
// THIS PAIR IS DELIBERATELY UNLAWFUL: SPEC §5.1 refuses a removed variant ("variant removed"). The file holds Gold,
// which this reader still names, so a leg that remaps ordinals by id LOADS it.
// So the lineage entry is handed in by the probe and never read
// from a lock. The NEW reader must refuse old_variant_removed.bin
// `layout_malformed` and write nothing (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.2, §5.4,
// §5.9 #30). Do not "fix" it.

package vold_variant_removed

enum Tier { Bronze, Silver, Gold }

fixed table VariantRemoved
{
    lead  uint32 = 1
    tier  Tier
    trail uint32 = 2
}
